ons into bullet points with clear action verbs at the beginning of each point.  This will make the information more concise and scannable. Use consistent formatting for all experience entries.  For example, use past tense verbs for completed projects and present tense for ongoing responsibilities."]}, {"title": "Skills", "description": "You\'ve listed a good range of relevant skills, including programming languages, frameworks, and tools.  This gives a clear picture of your technical capabilities. ", "ats_match": "90%", "recommendations": ["Organize your skills into categories, like \\"Programming Languages,\\" \\"Frameworks,\\" and \\"Tools.\\" This will make the information more structured and easy to read."]}, {"title": "Education", "description": "You\'ve included your educational background, which is relevant to your field.  However, consider adding details about your academic achievements.", "ats_match": "80%", "recommendations": ["Highlight any relevant coursework, projects, or awards related to your field.  For example, \\"Graduated with Honors in Computer Science\\" or \\"Developed a mobile application as a final year project.\\"  Consider adding a GPA if it\'s above average."}]}]}\n'}, 'file_uri': 'gs://genaiq_cloudbuild/uploads/OlusegunTewogbadeResume.pdf', 'filename': 'OlusegunTewogbadeResume.pdf'}>
