2024-09-05 16:22:42,197 - app - INFO - Session data after upload: <SecureCookieSession {'ai_response': {'overall_roast': "Olusesgun, you've got the ambition of a tech titan, the passion of a coding crusader, and the resume formatting skills of a… well, let's just say you could use some help in that department. It's like you're trying to write a novel on a 140-character tweet. Don't worry, though, everyone starts somewhere. We'll help you transform this resume from a chaotic symphony of information into a sleek, impactful, and ultimately more impressive masterpiece.  You've got the potential, but we need to unleash it with some strategic formatting and a little sprinkle of humor.", 'roast_cards': [{'description': "Olusesgun, the 'Greater Accra Region' feels more like a Craigslist ad than a professional designation. We get it, you're on the move, but we need a location, not a whole geographic area.  And the LinkedIn link?  It looks like you've had a run-in with the 'Shift' key, buddy.  Let's polish up that URL, and for goodness sake, put a space in 'te wogbade'.", 'recommendations': "Trade the 'Greater Accra Region' for a specific city. Fix that URL, and add a comma after your phone number - we don't want anyone thinking you're a phone number, even if it's a memorable one! Oh, and consider a professional headshot. It'll give recruiters a face to the name, which is a good thing, trust me. 😉", 'title': 'Contact Information'}, {'description': "Your summary reads like a passionate manifesto, Olusesgun, and I love the enthusiasm! But we need to cut through the jargon and highlight your greatest hits.  Remember, recruiters have limited attention spans, so they need a quick, punchy intro to grasp your value. This feels like you're explaining the entire plot of 'The Matrix' in a single paragraph.", 'recommendations': "Think about your top 3 skills or accomplishments.  What makes you stand out? Focus on quantifiable achievements and  use action verbs to make your impact clear.  For example, instead of 'solving real-world problems', say 'developed a [specific solution] that [quantifiable result]'. It's all about making your achievements sing! ", 'title': 'Summary'}, {'description': "Olusesgun, you're like a coding ninja! You've conquered technologies, tamed databases, and slayed bugs.  But this section needs some formatting TLC. The font is all over the place, and your descriptions are a bit long-winded. It's a tale of your triumphs, but it needs more structure.", 'recommendations': "Use bullet points to highlight your key responsibilities and achievements.  Make those descriptions concise and punchy.  Use numbers to quantify your accomplishments - 'reduced processing time by 40%' sounds much more impressive than 'streamlined event registration'.  And finally,  don't forget to include the company's location! It's important for recruiters to know where you've worked. ", 'title': 'Experience'}, {'description': "Olusesgun, this is a great list of skills, but it's like a buffet where everyone just piles their plate with everything.  Let's focus on the most relevant skills for the jobs you're applying to.  And if you're a master of those technologies,  don't be afraid to show off your expertise -  add a few details or  certifications to make your skills sing!", 'recommendations': "Group your skills into categories, like 'Programming Languages', 'Frameworks', 'Tools'.  Then, tailor your list to the specific job you're applying for.  For example,  if you're applying for a Python-focused role, highlight your Python experience and relevant projects. And if you're a certified ninja in a particular technology, flaunt that badge!", 'title': 'Skills'}, {'description': "Olusesgun, you've got the brains to match your coding prowess. But this section could use a little spice.  It's a bit bland, just stating the facts.  Let's inject some personality and highlight your academic achievements!", 'recommendations': "Add a line or two about your GPA, relevant coursework, or any academic awards or honors.  Did you create a groundbreaking project during your studies?  Showcase it!  It's your chance to shine beyond just the basics. ", 'title': 'Education'}, {'description': "Olusesgun, this is a good question, but it's  a bit awkward as a standalone section on your resume.  It's like asking a date to pick the restaurant before you've even asked them out!  This should be incorporated into your cover letter.  Your resume should be showcasing your skills, and the cover letter is the perfect place to connect those skills to the specific job.", 'recommendations': "Move this question to your cover letter.  Use this space to directly connect your skills and experience to the job requirements and show the hiring manager that you've done your research. It's the perfect opportunity to weave a narrative about why you're the ideal candidate. ", 'title': "Which of your achievements match the job you're applying to?"}]}, 'file_uri': 'gs://genaiq_cloudbuild/uploads/OlusegunTewogbadeResume.pdf', 'filename': 'OlusegunTewogbadeResume.pdf'}>
