2024-09-06 05:37:18,479 - app - INFO - Analysis result: {'introduction': "Alright, everybody, gather round! I've got a resume here that's got more typos than a toddler's first attempt at writing. This is like that friend who shows up to a party in a full suit, but their shirt's inside-out... and they're wearing flip-flops. It's trying so hard to impress, but it just... fails miserably. You ready for this? 'Cause this resume, it's about to get roasted so bad, it'll need a fire extinguisher. *Cue dramatic music* Let's begin...", 'steps': [{'header': 'First Impressions', 'description': "This resume is a textbook case of 'trying too hard.' It's got so many buzzwords, it sounds like a dictionary threw up on a keyboard.  And the formatting?  Don't even get me started. It's like a formatting tornado hit, then left a note saying, 'Sorry, I'm not good with spaces.'"}, {'header': 'Section-by-Section Roast', 'description': "Let's break down this masterpiece, shall we? The summary? It's like a motivational poster made into a job description.  'Passionate' is the word of the year, I guess.  The experience section reads like a laundry list of companies and accomplishments.  This isn't a resume, it's a 'Look at all the cool things I've done' infomercial. The skills?  Oh, the skills.  It's got everything from 'Java' to 'Git' to 'Jenkins.'  It's like, 'Hey, I can code.  But I can also use a computer.'  It's a masterpiece of mediocrity."}, {'header': 'Kevin Hart-isms', 'description': "You know what, I'm gonna 'keep it 100' with y'all.  This resume is like those friends who tell you they're 'successful' but they can't even spell 'entrepreneur' without Google.  You gon' learn today! *Kevin points dramatically at the resume*  This ain't about knowing a bunch of techy stuff.  It's about being able to communicate what you know.  And this, my friends, is a prime example of 'talkin' a big game, but not backin' it up.'"}, {'header': 'Physical Comedy', 'description': "If I saw this resume in person, I'd be running around the room, arms flailing, screaming 'What is this?! What. Is. This?!' It's got so much content, but it feels so hollow. It's like those cardboard cutouts they put up at car dealerships, all dressed up, but no substance. You gotta bring the energy, baby!  This resume needs more 'oomph.'"}, {'header': 'Real Talk', 'description': "Look, I'm gonna give you some real talk.  You gotta cut the fluff, stop trying to impress everyone with all these buzzwords.  Focus on what makes you unique.  Show them what you can actually do.  Don't be afraid to be yourself, even if it means being 'slightly' less impressive. You might just surprise yourself. And who knows, you might actually land that dream job.  Just ditch the 'motivational poster' vibe and be authentic.  That's the real secret sauce to landing a gig.  Trust me, it'll save you a lot of time and headaches."}]}
