2024-09-06 06:22:29,169 - app - INFO - Analysis result: {'introduction': "Yo, welcome to the 'Roast Me' show! Today's subject? This resume! It's so desperate for attention, it's practically wearing a 'Look at me!' sign... made of pixels, of course. This thing's got more buzzwords than a tech conference in Silicon Valley. Let's break it down, shall we?  But first, lemme just say... this is some serious 'I'm trying too hard' energy. It's like the resume equivalent of those dudes who wear their gym clothes everywhere, even to the grocery store. You gon' learn today! ", 'steps': [{'header': 'First Impressions', 'description': "It's like a frantic student who just crammed for a test. I mean, the guy's got a LinkedIn URL, a Twitter handle, and even a website for his side hustle. This ain't your average resume, folks. This is a full-blown marketing campaign! But, you know what's missing? A good ol' fashioned resume objective. You know, the thing that actually tells the recruiter what you're looking for.  You gon' learn today! *Kevin rubs his chin thoughtfully and makes a 'hm' noise*"}, {'header': 'Section-by-Section Roast', 'description': "Let's start with the 'Summary.' It's practically a love letter to every buzzword in the tech industry. Fintech, AI, mobile apps... it's like a word vomit session from a tech evangelist.  The 'Experience' section is a trip. This guy's a one-man tech army! He's done everything from building APIs to integrating AI chatbots.  He's even got a 'Lead Campus Ambassador' role for Ingressive for Good.  *Kevin does a dramatic hand gesture and snaps his fingers* You know what this tells me? This guy's got a serious case of 'FOMO' (Fear Of Missing Out). He's been to every conference, tried every tech stack, and done every side hustle.  But what about actually having a track record?  The 'Skills' section is a straight-up list of every programming language and framework under the sun. It's like the tech equivalent of a buffet.  *Kevin shakes his head and makes a 'tsk tsk' noise*  You know what they say... jack of all trades, master of none.  And finally, the 'Education' section.  'BSC Computer Science.'  *Kevin raises an eyebrow and smirks*  I mean, it's not a PhD in rocket science, but it'll do.  You gon' learn today!"}, {'header': 'Kevin Hart-isms', 'description': "This resume is so long, it's got a 'to be continued' at the bottom!  *Kevin looks around in disbelief and shakes his head*  This ain't a novel, dude! It's a resume! And this thing is more packed than a subway in rush hour.  *Kevin mimes riding a subway with exaggerated movements*  But the real kicker? This guy's got a 'Blue Vision Multimedia - BVM' gig...  *Kevin pauses and then whispers dramatically*  What is that even?  Blue Vision Multimedia?  I mean, the name alone makes me want to run for the hills!"}, {'header': 'Physical Comedy', 'description': "If I saw this resume in person, I'd be running around the room, arms flailing, screaming 'What is this?! What. Is. This?!'  *Kevin dramatically throws his arms in the air and stomps his feet*  This thing's got more acronyms than a NASA mission!  *Kevin makes a confused face and mimes reading a document with his finger*  I'm just trying to find the information I need, man.  I'm not trying to decipher a secret code! You gon' learn today!"}, {'header': 'Real Talk', 'description': "Look, I get it. You want to impress the recruiter. You want to show them you're a tech guru with all the latest skills. But sometimes, less is more.  *Kevin leans in and whispers*  Focus on the key skills and projects that actually matter for the job. And ditch the 'I'm a tech rockstar' attitude.  *Kevin gives a thumbs up*  Let your work speak for itself.  You gon' learn today!"}]}
