2024-09-06 06:27:23,279 - app - INFO - Analysis result: {'introduction': 'Alright, everybody! Gather round, \'cause I\'m \'bout to dissect this resume like a Thanksgiving turkey. It\'s so packed with buzzwords, it\'s practically a dictionary with a side of LinkedIn. We got \'passionate,\' \'impactful,\' \'innovative,\'—you name it, it\'s in here. But hold on, is this a resume or a mission statement for the United Nations of Software Development? I swear, I saw \'leading the team\' in a fortune cookie once.  We gon\' break down this thing, section by section, and I\'m not holding back. You gon\' learn today!"', 'steps': [{'header': 'First Impressions', 'description': "Yo, this thing's so long, it's like a Netflix show.  They got a whole story in here, from 'Fasyl Technology Group' to 'Blue Vision Media.' Did this guy write a novel instead of a resume? I'm just picturing a 'To Be Continued' sign at the bottom. And what's with the name?  OLUSEGUN TEW OGBADE?  Sound like the title of a Nigerian action film,  and that's not a bad thing, mind you. But this resume is so long, I bet it has its own theme music!"}, {'header': 'Section-by-Section Roast', 'description': "'EXPERIENCE'...  Wow, this guy is the ultimate side hustle king. It's like he's got a job for every day of the week.  But I'm confused—Consultant Programmer? Partner, CTO?  Is this guy a walking job description generator?  I swear, he's got more titles than a royal family.  And don't even get me started on the 'SKILLS' section. This guy knows every programming language under the sun. He's like a human compiler! Java, Python, Dart, SQL—I'm surprised he didn't list 'Morse Code' and 'Bird Whistling.' I'm pretty sure this resume is longer than the Bible, but at least I finally found a use for all those acronyms I learned in college.  And hey, 'Lead Ambassador'?  That's like the ultimate resume flex. I wonder if he gets paid in swag? Maybe a t-shirt that says 'I <3 Code'?"}, {'header': 'Kevin Hart-isms', 'description': "'I'm a passionate software developer...with a knack for fintech...'  Oh, really?  Is that what they call it these days?  A 'knack'?  I thought they were called 'skills'.  And don't even get me started on the whole 'AI' thing.  He's like, 'I'm an AI guru!  I can integrate AI into a toaster!'  I bet he sleeps in a t-shirt that says 'I Love AI'—I'd wear that shirt, too, if I could write code that could make me disappear from awkward situations.  And listen, 'making technology work for people'?  That's a noble goal, but have you heard of 'user experience'?  This guy's so focused on coding, he probably forgets that real people are using these things.  It's like, 'Yo, here's my code, now figure it out!'"}, {'header': 'Physical Comedy', 'description': "If I saw this resume in person, I'd be running around the room, arms flailing, screaming 'What is this?! What. Is. This?!'  It's like the resume equivalent of a clown car—all these skills and experiences just keep pouring out! I'd be doing a full-blown 'Kevin Hart dance'—you know, the one where I'm jumping up and down, pointing at the resume, and yelling, 'This is too much! This is too much!'"}, {'header': 'Real Talk', 'description': "Look,  I know this guy is talented,  but this resume is more about impressing than making connections.  Don't get caught up in the hype words.  Focus on showcasing what you can actually do for the company.  And for the love of all that is holy,  get rid of all the 'I' statements.  We get it, you're a software developer—but the real magic happens when you work with others.  So, ditch the ego, embrace the team, and let your skills do the talking. You gon' learn today!  And remember, I'm just kidding,  but also,  I'm not."}]}
