2024-09-06 06:32:07,908 - app - INFO - Session data after upload: <SecureCookieSession {'ai_response': {'introduction': "Alright, everybody, gather round! I've got a resume here that's got more typos than a toddler's first attempt at writing. This is like that friend who shows up to a party in a full suit, but their shirt's inside-out... and they're wearing flip-flops. It's trying so hard to impress, but it just... fails miserably. You ready for this? 'Cause this resume, it's about to get roasted so bad, it'll need a fire extinguisher. *Cue dramatic music* Let's begin...", 'steps': [{'description': "This resume is a textbook case of 'trying too hard.' It's got so many buzzwords, it sounds like a dictionary threw up on a keyboard.  And the formatting?  Don't even get me started. It's like a formatting tornado hit, then left a note saying, 'Sorry, I'm not good with spaces.'", 'header': 'First Impressions'}, {'description': "Let's break down this masterpiece, shall we? The summary? It's like a motivational poster made into a job description.  'Passionate' is the word of the year, I guess.  The experience section reads like a laundry list of companies and accomplishments.  This isn't a resume, it's a 'Look at all the cool things I've done' infomercial. The skills?  Oh, the skills.  It's got everything from 'Java' to 'Git' to 'Jenkins.'  It's like, 'Hey, I can code.  But I can also use a computer.'  It's a masterpiece of mediocrity.", 'header': 'Section-by-Section Roast'}, {'description': "You know what, I'm gonna 'keep it 100' with y'all.  This resume is like those friends who tell you they're 'successful' but they can't even spell 'entrepreneur' without Google.  You gon' learn today! *Kevin points dramatically at the resume*  This ain't about knowing a bunch of techy stuff.  It's about being able to communicate what you know.  And this, my friends, is a prime example of 'talkin' a big game, but not backin' it up.'", 'header': 'Kevin Hart-isms'}, {'description': "If I saw this resume in person, I'd be running around the room, arms flailing, screaming 'What is this?! What. Is. This?!' It's got so much content, but it feels so hollow. It's like those cardboard cutouts they put up at car dealerships, all dressed up, but no substance. You gotta bring the energy, baby!  This resume needs more 'oomph.'", 'header': 'Physical Comedy'}, {'description': "Look, I'm gonna give you some real talk.  You gotta cut the fluff, stop trying to impress everyone with all these buzzwords.  Focus on what makes you unique.  Show them what you can actually do.  Don't be afraid to be yourself, even if it means being 'slightly' less impressive. You might just surprise yourself. And who knows, you might actually land that dream job.  Just ditch the 'motivational poster' vibe and be authentic.  That's the real secret sauce to landing a gig.  Trust me, it'll save you a lot of time and headaches.", 'header': 'Real Talk'}]}, 'ai_roast_response': {'introduction': 'Alright, everybody! Gather round, \'cause I\'m \'bout to dissect this resume like a Thanksgiving turkey. It\'s so packed with buzzwords, it\'s practically a dictionary with a side of LinkedIn. We got \'passionate,\' \'impactful,\' \'innovative,\'—you name it, it\'s in here. But hold on, is this a resume or a mission statement for the United Nations of Software Development? I swear, I saw \'leading the team\' in a fortune cookie once.  We gon\' break down this thing, section by section, and I\'m not holding back. You gon\' learn today!"', 'steps': [{'description': "Yo, this thing's so long, it's like a Netflix show.  They got a whole story in here, from 'Fasyl Technology Group' to 'Blue Vision Media.' Did this guy write a novel instead of a resume? I'm just picturing a 'To Be Continued' sign at the bottom. And what's with the name?  OLUSEGUN TEW OGBADE?  Sound like the title of a Nigerian action film,  and that's not a bad thing, mind you. But this resume is so long, I bet it has its own theme music!", 'header': 'First Impressions'}, {'description': "'EXPERIENCE'...  Wow, this guy is the ultimate side hustle king. It's like he's got a job for every day of the week.  But I'm confused—Consultant Programmer? Partner, CTO?  Is this guy a walking job description generator?  I swear, he's got more titles than a royal family.  And don't even get me started on the 'SKILLS' section. This guy knows every programming language under the sun. He's like a human compiler! Java, Python, Dart, SQL—I'm surprised he didn't list 'Morse Code' and 'Bird Whistling.' I'm pretty sure this resume is longer than the Bible, but at least I finally found a use for all those acronyms I learned in college.  And hey, 'Lead Ambassador'?  That's like the ultimate resume flex. I wonder if he gets paid in swag? Maybe a t-shirt that says 'I <3 Code'?", 'header': 'Section-by-Section Roast'}, {'description': "'I'm a passionate software developer...with a knack for fintech...'  Oh, really?  Is that what they call it these days?  A 'knack'?  I thought they were called 'skills'.  And don't even get me started on the whole 'AI' thing.  He's like, 'I'm an AI guru!  I can integrate AI into a toaster!'  I bet he sleeps in a t-shirt that says 'I Love AI'—I'd wear that shirt, too, if I could write code that could make me disappear from awkward situations.  And listen, 'making technology work for people'?  That's a noble goal, but have you heard of 'user experience'?  This guy's so focused on coding, he probably forgets that real people are using these things.  It's like, 'Yo, here's my code, now figure it out!'", 'header': 'Kevin Hart-isms'}, {'description': "If I saw this resume in person, I'd be running around the room, arms flailing, screaming 'What is this?! What. Is. This?!'  It's like the resume equivalent of a clown car—all these skills and experiences just keep pouring out! I'd be doing a full-blown 'Kevin Hart dance'—you know, the one where I'm jumping up and down, pointing at the resume, and yelling, 'This is too much! This is too much!'", 'header': 'Physical Comedy'}, {'description': "Look,  I know this guy is talented,  but this resume is more about impressing than making connections.  Don't get caught up in the hype words.  Focus on showcasing what you can actually do for the company.  And for the love of all that is holy,  get rid of all the 'I' statements.  We get it, you're a software developer—but the real magic happens when you work with others.  So, ditch the ego, embrace the team, and let your skills do the talking. You gon' learn today!  And remember, I'm just kidding,  but also,  I'm not.", 'header': 'Real Talk'}]}, 'file_uri': 'gs://genaiq_cloudbuild/uploads/Olusegun_Tewogbade.pdf', 'filename': 'Olusegun_Tewogbade.pdf'}>
