2024-09-06 06:32:18,058 - app - INFO - Analysis result: {'introduction': "Yo, hold up! I see this resume and my first thought is, 'Did this guy write this on a napkin after a couple of beers at a tech conference?'  Man, this resume is so desperate to impress, it's practically doing a lap dance for recruiters. Let's break this bad boy down, shall we? It's about to get real, real funny. You gon' learn today!", 'steps': [{'header': 'First Impressions', 'description': "This resume is a textbook case of trying too hard. It's like a kid who just learned how to use bold and italics and wants to show off every single time.  We got the full name, multiple titles, and enough contact info to start a small phone company.  It's like the resume equivalent of wearing a suit to a barbecue.  What's next?  A resume in Comic Sans?  Get a grip, man! "}, {'header': 'Summary', 'description': "This 'summary' is more of a 'summary of why I'm trying to hide my lack of real experience'. It's filled with buzzwords and phrases like 'passionate software developer' and 'solving real-world problems'. It's like saying you're a 'creative writer' when you only write grocery lists.  Just say what you actually do, don't try to impress with words you barely understand."}, {'header': 'Experience', 'description': "This experience section is like a train wreck in slow motion.  It's a laundry list of  jobs, but instead of highlighting accomplishments, it's just a bunch of jargon and vague claims.  'Integrated Kafka to resolve delays...reduced response times by 60%'.  Dude, you're either making stuff up or you're just really bad at explaining what you actually do.  'Transitioned several services from Python Flask to Java Spring Boot'.  Is this a resume or a tech blog?  And don't get me started on the 'Abeyie Innovation Studios' bit.  Sounds like a place where they invent new ways to make coffee, not solve real problems. And the 'Blue Vision Multimedia - BVM' gig?  That name is so generic, I'm pretty sure it's already taken by a thousand other companies."}, {'header': 'Education', 'description': "Catholic University College, Ghana?  I don't know about you, but I'm getting a 'Catholic School' vibe from this.  Like, is there a prayer circle before every coding session?  Don't worry, we all got that one friend who went to a school with a funny name.  Just make sure it's relevant to the job you're applying for, because a degree in 'Computer Science' is about as useful as a degree in 'underwater basket weaving' if you don't have the skills to back it up."}, {'header': 'Skills', 'description': "This skills section is like a kid's first attempt at writing a shopping list.  'Java Python Dart SQL PL/SQL JavaScript'.  Ok, buddy, we get it, you know some coding stuff. But is this a grocery store or a tech company?  'Spring Boot Angular Flutter Flask'.  You know what this reminds me of?  A bunch of friends trying to impress their parents by throwing around fancy words they barely understand.  Here's a tip:  Instead of listing every random skill you've ever touched, pick a few that are actually relevant to the job you're applying for."}, {'header': 'Kevin Hart-isms', 'description': "You know, I'm starting to think this guy is trying to be the 'Kevin Hart of tech'.  He's got all the energy and enthusiasm of a chihuahua on a sugar rush, but without the comedic timing.  And the way he describes every accomplishment is like he's telling a story, but it's a story with no punchline.  'Increased trader decision accuracy by {30%}'.  What, are you a fortune teller now?  And this 'AI-driven solutions' thing is just a fancy way of saying you're still learning the basics.  It's like saying you're a 'master chef' because you know how to boil water."}, {'header': 'Physical Comedy', 'description': "If I saw this resume in person, I'd be running around the room, arms flailing, screaming 'What is this?! What. Is. This?!'  Then I'd grab the resume and start shaking it like a maraca, saying 'This is all you got?  This is all you got?  Come on, man, step it up!'"}]}
