2024-09-06 06:39:25,374 - app - INFO - Analysis result: {'introduction': "Yo, check out this resume! It's so long it makes my head spin like a washing machine on high speed.  My man's got more bullet points than a bulletproof vest.  And the font?  It's like he's trying to shout at you from across the room, 'Hey, look at me, I'm a software developer! I'm a software developer!'.  Dude, chill out.  We get it.", 'steps': [{'header': 'First Impressions', 'description': "This resume is like a Nigerian prince email - full of promises, but you can't help but feel like you're about to get scammed.  This dude is throwing every buzzword at the wall, hoping something sticks.  Fintech? Check. AI? Check. Flutter?  Check.  I'm pretty sure he's about to list 'breathing' as a skill. You gon' learn today!  But learn what, I'm not sure."}, {'header': 'Section-by-Section Roast', 'description': 'Let\'s start with "Experience." It\'s like a poorly organized garage sale - you\'ve got a bunch of random items, but nothing seems to belong together.  "Consultant Programmer"? Sounds more like a side hustle than a career. And "Partner, CTO"? I\'m guessing that means he\'s the boss of like, three other people.  I\'d be more impressed if he actually knew what a CTO does.  As for the "Skills" section, it\'s a basic tech sampler platter.  He\'s got everything, but does he really master anything?  I\'m guessing not.  It\'s like a wannabe chef who throws everything in the pot and hopes it tastes good.'}, {'header': 'Kevin Hart-isms', 'description': '\'I\'m dedicated to solving real-world problems and making technology work for people\'.... Yeah, dude, we all are.  That\'s kinda the point of being a software developer.  But you don\'t have to say it with the same dramatic flair as a Shakespearean actor. And \'significally boosting overall system responsiveness and scalability\' - are you writing a technical manual or a rap song?  Choose one.  And hey, don\'t forget about the "Education" section.  Catholic University College, Ghana?  Sounds like a nice place.  But that doesn\'t mean you gotta list it like it\'s the Sorbonne.'}, {'header': 'Physical Comedy', 'description': "If I saw this resume in person, I'd be running around the room, arms flailing, screaming 'What is this?! What. Is. This?!'   Like a dog chasing its tail, but instead of a tail, it's a laundry list of buzzwords and self-aggrandizing claims.  Someone, please, give this guy a thesaurus!  Or maybe just a reality check.  And I'm not even gonna mention the weird, half-assed URL he's using.  Did his website designer just give up halfway through?"}, {'header': 'Real Talk', 'description': "Yo, listen up.  This resume is a good start, but it needs a major overhaul.  Take out the fluff, focus on the skills that actually matter, and ditch the 'I'm-so-important' attitude.  And while you're at it,  get yourself a professional resume writer.  They can help you translate all that tech mumbo jumbo into something that actually makes sense to a hiring manager.  Don't be afraid to be yourself, but be a confident, competent, and professional yourself.  You got this! Now go out there and get that job, dude!  But no more 'AI-driven solutions', please.  Just keep it real."}]}
