2024-09-07 05:19:46,293 - app - INFO - Analysis result: {'introduction': "Alright, everybody, settle down! We got a resume here that's so packed with buzzwords, it's practically vibrating!  This ain't a resume, it's a freakin' marketing campaign for the 'Software Developer' brand.  You gon' learn today!  Listen up, cause this roast is gonna be hotter than a Ghanaian summer and funnier than a Nigerian wedding.", 'step': [{'header': 'First Impressions', 'description': "This resume is like a Nigerian restaurant menu – it promises you the world but then you get a plate of beans and fufu.  It's got all the right words, but it's missing the real heart and soul.  It's like a  'build your own'  burger:  lots of potential, but still ain't got that special sauce to make it really pop."}, {'header': 'Section-by-Section Roast', 'description': "Let's dissect this thing, piece by piece, like a hungry lion on a gazelle!  First, we got the 'Summary'.  This is supposed to be your 'elevator pitch', but it sounds like a robot reciting a dictionary definition of 'software developer'.  Where's the personality?  Where's the passion?  Maybe swap out 'impactful solutions' for 'awesome code' and 'real-world problems' for 'helping people' – you know, like actual human stuff.\n\nNow, let's take a look at 'Experience'.  'Consultant Programmer',  'Software Developer',  'Partner, CTO' –  oh, honey, it's a career that's just begging for a reality show.  'Fasyl Technology Group' – that name sounds like someone's trying to pronounce 'fast food' with a mouthful of peanuts.  But hey, they got an 'ACH' system and 'electronic alerts'  –  sounds more like they're running a spam factory than a fintech company.  And 'Blue Vision Multimedia' – did they hire their naming team at a blindfold dart game?  They're in the 'Greater Accra Region' – you mean like, where they filmed 'Black Panther'?\n\nSpeaking of 'Education',  'Catholic University College, Ghana' –  we got a tech guru with a background in liturgical studies.  He's probably coding prayers in Java, right?\n\nAnd let's not forget the 'Skills' section!  'Programming Languages':  Java, Python, Dart, SQL, PL/SQL, JavaScript –  this dude's got a bigger vocabulary than a Shakespearean play.  But hold on,  'Frameworks and Libraries':  Spring Boot, Angular, Flutter, Flask  –  it's a laundry list of everything he's ever heard of.  And then the 'Tools and Platforms':  Kafka, Git, Jenkins –  he's got every tool in the shed, but is he actually building anything useful?  It's like he went to the software developer grocery store and just threw every item in his basket.  You gon' learn today!  This resume needs a serious detox – too much caffeine, not enough creativity.  It's like a tech version of the 'I'm with the band' T-shirt. "}, {'header': 'Kevin Hart-isms', 'description': "This resume?  It's so boring, I'm  'almost asleep right now'.  You know, I'm a  'really, really, really'  big fan of good resumes.  This one,  'it's not that good' .  This is like a tech version of a  'white shirt, black pants'  outfit –  safe, but ain't turning heads.   You gotta give me something  'spicy',  something that makes me want to say  'Oh!  Snap!'"}, {'header': 'Physical Comedy', 'description': "If I saw this resume in person, I'd be doing a  'running man'  dance around the room, like  'This thing is so dry, it's giving me a dust allergy!  This resume is so weak, it's making me question the existence of gravity!'"}, {'header': 'Real Talk', 'description': "Look, I'm gonna give you some real talk –  you got the skills, you got the experience, but you gotta make it sizzle!  Show me your personality, your passion.  Don't be afraid to be bold, be creative.  And for the love of all things tech, ditch the buzzwords.  This ain't a  'tech speak dictionary',  this is your story.  Tell it with your own voice, your own flair.   You got this, I believe in you. Now go out there and show 'em what you're made of!"}]}
