2024-09-07 05:24:02,859 - app - INFO - Analysis result: {'introduction': "Alright, folks, gather 'round! This resume is so long, it probably needs its own zip code. And the title? 'Software Developer'? Honey, you're about as close to a 'Software Developer' as I am to being a professional ballerina. I mean, you might be able to write code, but judging by this resume, your English skills need a major upgrade. It's like trying to understand a foreign language with a broken dictionary. This is Kevin Hart's 'what's the most polite way to say someone's resume is a hot mess' roast. Buckle up, because this is gonna be a wild ride.", 'First Impressions': {'header': 'First Impressions: A Visual Disaster', 'description': "Yo, first glance? This thing is screaming 'I googled 'how to make a resume' and then just typed everything I could find.' It's a hodgepodge of fonts, formatting, and general chaos.  And this font? It's like it was designed for a 90's web page. It screams 'I'm trying to be professional, but I'm actually a meme.'  If I saw this resume in person, I'd be running around the room, arms flailing, screaming 'What is this?! What. Is. This?!''"}, 'Section-by-Section Roast': {'header': 'Section-by-Section: A Comedy of Errors', 'description': "Let's break down this masterpiece, shall we? Starting with the 'Summary':  'I'm a passionate software developer.'  Honey, where's the passion?  I see more passion in a bowl of lukewarm oatmeal. 'Fintech, AI, and mobile app development.'  Sounds impressive, but I'm still waiting for the proof. You got more skills than a Swiss Army knife, but this resume ain't showcasing 'em.  Next up, the 'Experience' section. It's like a novel that's missing the plot. There's a lot of talk about  'solutions,'  'systems,' and 'integration,' but none of it actually tells me what you did.  Did you actually build anything? Did you break anything?  We need specifics, my friend.  And the 'Education' section?  'BSC Computer Science.'  Congratulations! But please tell me, did you actually *learn* anything in those four years? Or were you just busy learning how to use emojis in your emails?   And the skills?  'Java, Python, Dart, SQL, PL/SQL, JavaScript.'  Yeah, we get it, you can code.  Now show us you can actually write a resume that doesn't make me want to hurl.  You gon' learn today!"}, 'Kevin Hart-isms': {'header': "Kevin Hart-isms: Where's the Laugh Track?", 'description': "You know, I'm all about the hustle. But this resume is making me feel like I'm in a marathon… where everyone else is running towards the finish line, and you're just standing there, waving a flag.  'Leading a team?'  Honey, I've seen teams that are more cohesive than that.  'AI'?  You're using 'AI' like it's some magic word that's gonna solve all your problems. It's like saying 'I'm a good cook' and then serving your guests burnt toast.  And the 'electronic alerts'?  Don't get me started on the 'electronic alerts.'  They're so spammy, they should come with a free subscription to Gmail.  You gon' learn today!"}, 'Physical Comedy': {'header': 'Physical Comedy: This Resume is My New Workout', 'description': "If I tried to read this resume out loud, my voice would crack from all the awkward pauses.  I'd be doing a full body workout just trying to make it through all the filler words.  And the constant bragging about 'integrating' and 'optimizing'?  It's like nails on a chalkboard.  You gon' learn today!"}, 'Real Talk': {'header': 'Real Talk: Time to Get Real', 'description': "Look, I know you're trying, but this resume ain't doing you any favors.  It's like a clown trying to be a comedian—you're trying too hard, and it's not landing.  Focus on what you're good at, what makes you unique, and let that shine through.  Make it short, sweet, and to the point.  And for the love of all that is holy, get rid of this font.  You gon' learn today!"}}
