2024-09-07 05:28:06,045 - app - INFO - Session data after upload: <SecureCookieSession {'ai_roast_response': {'introduction': "Alright, alright, alright! Gather 'round, folks, 'cause we got a resume here that's about as exciting as watching paint dry. You know that feeling when you see a restaurant menu with just 'fish' on it?  Yeah, that's this resume. It's so vague, you could write your own story about this guy.  It's like he's trying to be a tech version of 'The Da Vinci Code' - full of mystery and leaving you with more questions than answers.  But hey, maybe it's a good thing he's a 'Software Developer' because he sure can't write a resume. You gon' learn today! ", 'step': [{'description': "This resume is the definition of 'trying too hard'. It's like a high schooler trying to act like they're a grown-up.  It's so packed with buzzwords it's practically vibrating. 'Impactful solutions,' 'real-world problems,' 'dedicated to solving...,'  Seriously,  dude, just chill.  You sound like a robot trying to write like a human.  And the way he's describing himself as passionate? You'd think he's inventing the wheel, not just writing code.  Let's be honest, this resume's so desperate, it's practically begging for a job.  It's like a lost dog, just hoping someone will give it a pat on the head.", 'header': 'First Impressions'}, {'description': "Let's start with the 'Experience' section.  This dude's got a job title for every year of his life, but I ain't seeing any real achievements.  He's 'Developed and deployed RESTful APIs' - yeah, me too, I did that last night while ordering pizza.  He's 'Led the implementation and deployment of eAlert service' - so, he basically set up a notification system.   I'm not saying it's not impressive, but  he's bragging about things that are kinda standard in the tech world.  And don't get me started on 'Blue Vision Multimedia - BVM.'  That sounds like a side hustle I'd do on a Saturday night.  We gotta talk about the education section too.  'BSC Computer Science, CATHOLIC UNIVERSITY COLLEGE, GHANA'.  I'm not dissing his alma mater, but is that the only university in Ghana?  And how is he going to stand out when all he has to show is a generic college degree?  You gon' learn today!  He's got 'Skills' listed, but I'm not seeing any quantifiable results.  Java, Python, Dart, SQL -  cool, but what can you actually do with them?  This whole resume is just a bunch of generic keywords thrown together.   It's like he's trying to impress me with his vocabulary, but all he's doing is showing me he has no personality.", 'header': 'Section-by-Section Roast'}, {'description': "You know, I'm just picturing this guy in an interview, sweating bullets, trying to sound confident, and the interviewer is just staring at him like, 'Are you kidding me?'  He's trying to sell himself as this unstoppable force in tech, but all he's doing is making me laugh.  I mean, he's like a one-man comedy show, but not in a good way.  This resume is so bad, it's actually good. It's like that friend who always tells the worst jokes, but you can't help but laugh.  So yeah, this resume might not be a masterpiece, but it's definitely got some entertainment value.  And honestly, that's all I really need.  You gon' learn today! ", 'header': 'Kevin Hart-isms'}]}, 'file_uri': 'gs://genaiq_cloudbuild/uploads/Olusegun_Tewogbade.pdf', 'filename': 'Olusegun_Tewogbade.pdf'}>
