2024-09-07 05:28:12,863 - app - INFO - Analysis result: {'introduction': "Yo! So, this resume is like a Nigerian street vendor trying to sell you a mixtape...it's loud, it's flashy, and it's trying way too hard to be something it's not.  But hold up, let's break it down like a hot plate of suya.", 'steps': [{'header': 'First Impressions', 'description': "Right off the bat, this thing is more cluttered than a Lagos market after a power outage.  We got links, we got social media handles, we got more bold font than a Nigerian grandma's birthday invitation.  It's trying so hard to be impressive that it's practically begging for a 'humble brag' award.  It's like, 'Look at me!  Look at all the things I do!  I'm so important!' But, honestly, this resume is about as impressive as a broken generator in the middle of a heatwave.  This dude's got a whole lot of 'I'm busy' energy but not enough 'I actually got results' energy.  It's like he's trying to sell me a story before he's even written the first chapter."}, {'header': 'Basketmouth Impressions', 'description': "You know what they say? 'You gon' learn today!'  Let's see, Java, Python, Dart... 'Yaaaaaa' - sounds like he's trying to impress every coding bootcamp in existence.  But hey, maybe he's just trying to show off his 'superpower' - the ability to know every programming language except the one he's actually good at.  *Laughs hysterically* And Flutter?  Seriously?  Did they give out free Flutter certification at the local market because this guy's got it listed like it's some kind of miracle.  And look, 'Kafka' - oh, here comes the expert!  He's got Kafka like it's a new pair of Yeezy's!  Let me tell you, 'Kafka' is not a magic word.  It's like saying 'I know how to use a semicolon' - it's just basic coding stuff, dude.  Don't act like you're some tech guru.  You gon' learn today!"}]}
