s your ability to contribute to real-world projects. However, it could be strengthened by adding specific quantifiable achievements and impacts.", 'ats_match': '75%', 'recommendations': ["Instead of just listing tasks, quantify your achievements using numbers and metrics. For example, 'Developed a UI that increased user engagement by 15%.', 'Created a system that streamlined accounting processes, saving 10% in operational costs.'"]}, {'title': 'Academic Background', 'description': 'This section provides a clear overview of your academic credentials and demonstrates your specialization in software development.  Highlighting your focus on software development and mentioning relevant coursework or projects could further strengthen this section.', 'ats_match': '70%', 'recommendations': ["Consider adding relevant coursework or projects that align with your career aspirations. For example, 'Completed a project on building a real-time data analytics platform using Python and Django.'"]}, {'title': 'Personal Projects', 'description': 'This section demonstrates your passion for software development and your desire to explore new technologies. It showcases your ability to take initiative and work independently.', 'ats_match': '65%', 'recommendations': ["Expand on the details of your projects, providing more context and emphasizing the skills you gained. For example, 'Developed a face mask detector using OpenCV and Python, achieving 95% accuracy in identifying masks.'", 'Include links to your project repositories, like your Github account, to showcase your work more effectively.']}]}
